{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Tb4e5JWVN7v3JYmYhzzXJ7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** GNU coreutils have no formal specifications accessible to implementers. This project derives specifications from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** A four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds one Go binary per utility, `pkg/` provides shared infrastructure (testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil), and `docs/specs/` holds the SRDs that drive code generation.\n\n**Current state:** 33 releases specified (00.0–15.0), covering 111 utilities. Many utilities are implemented (most of releases 00.0–10.1), but significant gaps remain. The most recent commits implemented `cmd/mkfifo` (srd092 R1.x and R2.x).\n\n**Current focus:** The `requirement_states` field shows which SRD requirements are \"ready\" for task proposals. The earliest incomplete release with ready requirements is **11.0** (mknod, nice, nohup — mkfifo is already implemented).\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 11.0 has 3 remaining utilities: mknod (srd093), nice (srd094), nohup (srd095). All requirements are \"ready\". Following the 4-task limit, I'll cover mknod (2 tasks) and nice (2 tasks). Nohup defers to the next batch.\n\nTasks 0 and 2 are independent (different utilities); tasks 1 and 3 depend on their respective core tasks.\n\n## Weight Budget Check\n\n```\nTask 0: srd093 R1.1 (w=1) + R1.2 (w=1) + R1.3 (w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 1: srd093 R2.1 (w=1) + R2.2 (w=1) + R2.3 (w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 2: srd094 R1.1 (w=1) + R1.2 (w=1) + R1.3 (w=1) + R1.4 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 3: srd094 R2.1 (w=1) + R2.2 (w=1) + R2.3 (w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/mknod core special file creation and mode setting (srd093 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd093-mknod.yaml (requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3)\n      - cmd/mkfifo/main.go (reference implementation for similar special file creation utility)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/mknod/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: mknod utility -- creates block special, character special, or FIFO special files\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd093 R1.1 -- argument parsing for mknod NAME TYPE [MAJOR MINOR] with --help and --version support\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd093 R1.2 -- create block special (b), character special (c/u), and FIFO (p) file types using appropriate syscalls with correct device number handling\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd093 R1.3 -- mode setting via -m/--mode flag with proper umask interaction for created special files\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project shared protocol\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use syscall.Mknod for block and character special file creation with major/minor device number encoding\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Build output binary to bin/mknod using go build -o bin/mknod ./cmd/mknod/\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/mknod/main.go compiles without errors: go build ./cmd/mknod/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/mknod/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"mknod creates FIFO files when TYPE is p without requiring MAJOR/MINOR arguments\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"mknod creates block and character special files with correct device numbers when TYPE is b or c/u\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"mknod applies -m/--mode flag to set permissions on created files\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/mknod error handling and differential tests (srd093 R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd093-mknod.yaml (requirements R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\n      - cmd/mknod/main.go (core implementation from previous task)\n      - cmd/mkfifo/mkfifo_test.go (reference test file for differential testing pattern)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing framework -- BuildBinary, RunDiffTests, DiffTest)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/mknod/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add error handling for invalid arguments, missing device numbers, and filesystem errors\n      - path: cmd/mknod/mknod_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests comparing Go mknod against gmknod reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd093 R2.1 -- error handling for invalid or missing arguments with correct stderr messages and exit codes matching GNU mknod\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd093 R2.2 -- error handling for filesystem errors (permission denied, file already exists, invalid device numbers)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd093 R2.3 -- differential tests against gmknod reference binary using testutils.RunDiffTests covering success and error paths\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use testutils.BuildBinary(t, \\\".\\\") to compile the Go binary for testing\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Call exec.LookPath(\\\"gmknod\\\") and t.Skip if the reference binary is not found\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Test cases cover FIFO creation, invalid type arguments, missing MAJOR/MINOR for block/char types, and --help/--version output\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/mknod/ -count=1 passes with no failures\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Differential tests compare exit code, stdout, and stderr against gmknod for each test case\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Tests skip gracefully when gmknod is not in PATH via t.Skip\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Error messages and exit codes match GNU mknod behavior for all error paths\"\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/nice core priority adjustment and command execution (srd094 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd094-nice.yaml (requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage)\n      - cmd/mkfifo/main.go (reference for argument parsing and exit code patterns in cmd/ utilities)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/nice/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: nice utility -- runs a command with adjusted scheduling priority\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd094 R1.1 -- argument parsing for nice [-n ADJUSTMENT] [COMMAND [ARG...]] with --help and --version support\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd094 R1.2 -- default priority adjustment of +10 when no -n flag is provided\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd094 R1.3 -- custom adjustment via -n/--adjustment flag accepting positive and negative integer values\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd094 R1.4 -- execute the specified command with the adjusted nice value, preserving the command's exit code\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project shared protocol\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use syscall.Setpriority and syscall.Getpriority for nice value adjustment\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Match GNU nice exit code conventions -- 125 for nice itself failing, 126 if command found but not executable, 127 if command not found, otherwise the command's exit code\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Use syscall.Exec to replace the process with the command, matching GNU nice behavior\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/nice/main.go compiles without errors: go build ./cmd/nice/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/nice/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"nice with no -n flag applies default +10 adjustment\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"nice -n 5 COMMAND adjusts priority by +5 before executing COMMAND\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"The executed command's exit code is preserved and returned by nice\"\n\n- index: 3\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/nice error handling and differential tests (srd094 R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\"\n  dependency: 2\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd094-nice.yaml (requirements R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\n      - cmd/nice/main.go (core implementation from previous task)\n      - cmd/mkfifo/mkfifo_test.go (reference test file for differential testing pattern)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing framework -- BuildBinary, RunDiffTests, DiffTest)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/nice/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add error handling for invalid adjustment values and command execution failures\n      - path: cmd/nice/nice_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests comparing Go nice against gnice reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd094 R2.1 -- error handling for invalid adjustment values (non-numeric, out of range) with correct stderr messages\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd094 R2.2 -- error handling for command not found (exit 127) and command not executable (exit 126)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd094 R2.3 -- differential tests against gnice reference binary using testutils.RunDiffTests covering default adjustment, custom adjustment, invalid values, and command errors\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use testutils.BuildBinary(t, \\\".\\\") to compile the Go binary for testing\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Call exec.LookPath(\\\"gnice\\\") and t.Skip if the reference binary is not found\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Test cases cover default +10 adjustment, custom -n values, invalid adjustment strings, nonexistent commands, and --help/--version output\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/nice/ -count=1 passes with no failures\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Differential tests compare exit code, stdout, and stderr against gnice for each test case\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Tests skip gracefully when gnice is not in PATH via t.Skip\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Exit codes 125, 126, 127 match GNU nice behavior for respective error conditions\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46014,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46014},"output_tokens":29,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca1ea1ea-cd59-4793-9611-dee9c5a656b7","uuid":"496c112f-be9d-43ac-9297-b124d9647447"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":216205,"duration_api_ms":218085,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** GNU coreutils have no formal specifications accessible to implementers. This project derives specifications from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** A four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds one Go binary per utility, `pkg/` provides shared infrastructure (testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil), and `docs/specs/` holds the SRDs that drive code generation.\n\n**Current state:** 33 releases specified (00.0–15.0), covering 111 utilities. Many utilities are implemented (most of releases 00.0–10.1), but significant gaps remain. The most recent commits implemented `cmd/mkfifo` (srd092 R1.x and R2.x).\n\n**Current focus:** The `requirement_states` field shows which SRD requirements are \"ready\" for task proposals. The earliest incomplete release with ready requirements is **11.0** (mknod, nice, nohup — mkfifo is already implemented).\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 11.0 has 3 remaining utilities: mknod (srd093), nice (srd094), nohup (srd095). All requirements are \"ready\". Following the 4-task limit, I'll cover mknod (2 tasks) and nice (2 tasks). Nohup defers to the next batch.\n\nTasks 0 and 2 are independent (different utilities); tasks 1 and 3 depend on their respective core tasks.\n\n## Weight Budget Check\n\n```\nTask 0: srd093 R1.1 (w=1) + R1.2 (w=1) + R1.3 (w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 1: srd093 R2.1 (w=1) + R2.2 (w=1) + R2.3 (w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 2: srd094 R1.1 (w=1) + R1.2 (w=1) + R1.3 (w=1) + R1.4 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 3: srd094 R2.1 (w=1) + R2.2 (w=1) + R2.3 (w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/mknod core special file creation and mode setting (srd093 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd093-mknod.yaml (requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3)\n      - cmd/mkfifo/main.go (reference implementation for similar special file creation utility)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/mknod/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: mknod utility -- creates block special, character special, or FIFO special files\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd093 R1.1 -- argument parsing for mknod NAME TYPE [MAJOR MINOR] with --help and --version support\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd093 R1.2 -- create block special (b), character special (c/u), and FIFO (p) file types using appropriate syscalls with correct device number handling\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd093 R1.3 -- mode setting via -m/--mode flag with proper umask interaction for created special files\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project shared protocol\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use syscall.Mknod for block and character special file creation with major/minor device number encoding\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Build output binary to bin/mknod using go build -o bin/mknod ./cmd/mknod/\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/mknod/main.go compiles without errors: go build ./cmd/mknod/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/mknod/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"mknod creates FIFO files when TYPE is p without requiring MAJOR/MINOR arguments\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"mknod creates block and character special files with correct device numbers when TYPE is b or c/u\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"mknod applies -m/--mode flag to set permissions on created files\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/mknod error handling and differential tests (srd093 R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd093-mknod.yaml (requirements R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\n      - cmd/mknod/main.go (core implementation from previous task)\n      - cmd/mkfifo/mkfifo_test.go (reference test file for differential testing pattern)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing framework -- BuildBinary, RunDiffTests, DiffTest)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/mknod/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add error handling for invalid arguments, missing device numbers, and filesystem errors\n      - path: cmd/mknod/mknod_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests comparing Go mknod against gmknod reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd093 R2.1 -- error handling for invalid or missing arguments with correct stderr messages and exit codes matching GNU mknod\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd093 R2.2 -- error handling for filesystem errors (permission denied, file already exists, invalid device numbers)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd093 R2.3 -- differential tests against gmknod reference binary using testutils.RunDiffTests covering success and error paths\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use testutils.BuildBinary(t, \\\".\\\") to compile the Go binary for testing\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Call exec.LookPath(\\\"gmknod\\\") and t.Skip if the reference binary is not found\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Test cases cover FIFO creation, invalid type arguments, missing MAJOR/MINOR for block/char types, and --help/--version output\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/mknod/ -count=1 passes with no failures\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Differential tests compare exit code, stdout, and stderr against gmknod for each test case\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Tests skip gracefully when gmknod is not in PATH via t.Skip\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Error messages and exit codes match GNU mknod behavior for all error paths\"\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/nice core priority adjustment and command execution (srd094 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd094-nice.yaml (requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage)\n      - cmd/mkfifo/main.go (reference for argument parsing and exit code patterns in cmd/ utilities)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/nice/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: nice utility -- runs a command with adjusted scheduling priority\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd094 R1.1 -- argument parsing for nice [-n ADJUSTMENT] [COMMAND [ARG...]] with --help and --version support\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd094 R1.2 -- default priority adjustment of +10 when no -n flag is provided\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd094 R1.3 -- custom adjustment via -n/--adjustment flag accepting positive and negative integer values\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd094 R1.4 -- execute the specified command with the adjusted nice value, preserving the command's exit code\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project shared protocol\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use syscall.Setpriority and syscall.Getpriority for nice value adjustment\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Match GNU nice exit code conventions -- 125 for nice itself failing, 126 if command found but not executable, 127 if command not found, otherwise the command's exit code\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Use syscall.Exec to replace the process with the command, matching GNU nice behavior\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/nice/main.go compiles without errors: go build ./cmd/nice/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/nice/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"nice with no -n flag applies default +10 adjustment\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"nice -n 5 COMMAND adjusts priority by +5 before executing COMMAND\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"The executed command's exit code is preserved and returned by nice\"\n\n- index: 3\n  title: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/nice error handling and differential tests (srd094 R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\"\n  dependency: 2\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd094-nice.yaml (requirements R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\n      - cmd/nice/main.go (core implementation from previous task)\n      - cmd/mkfifo/mkfifo_test.go (reference test file for differential testing pattern)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing framework -- BuildBinary, RunDiffTests, DiffTest)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/nice/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add error handling for invalid adjustment values and command execution failures\n      - path: cmd/nice/nice_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests comparing Go nice against gnice reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd094 R2.1 -- error handling for invalid adjustment values (non-numeric, out of range) with correct stderr messages\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd094 R2.2 -- error handling for command not found (exit 127) and command not executable (exit 126)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd094 R2.3 -- differential tests against gnice reference binary using testutils.RunDiffTests covering default adjustment, custom adjustment, invalid values, and command errors\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use testutils.BuildBinary(t, \\\".\\\") to compile the Go binary for testing\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Call exec.LookPath(\\\"gnice\\\") and t.Skip if the reference binary is not found\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Test cases cover default +10 adjustment, custom -n values, invalid adjustment strings, nonexistent commands, and --help/--version output\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/nice/ -count=1 passes with no failures\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Differential tests compare exit code, stdout, and stderr against gnice for each test case\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Tests skip gracefully when gnice is not in PATH via t.Skip\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Exit codes 125, 126, 127 match GNU nice behavior for respective error conditions\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ca1ea1ea-cd59-4793-9611-dee9c5a656b7","total_cost_usd":0.6668059999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46014,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":13503,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46014,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":13503,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46014,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46014},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":35628,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.035713,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":13503,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":46014,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6310929999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_